@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+# CPPN sequence test (2026-11-01)
+
+Question: when fitted dense CPPNs learn local edits in sequence, how much do they forget, and how much replay holds it down?
+
+Pre-registered in `seed_kb.json` by the commit that adds this file, before any full run. Results live outside this
+repository, in the lab directory, because `*.jsonl` and `**/results/` are not tracked here.
+
+    export AIQ_CPPN_PYTHON=<interpreter with a GPU> AIQ_CPPN_ASSETS=<dir with genomes/ and nets/>
+    PYTHONPATH=src python -m aiq_kb.kb_cppn run LAB_DIR
+    PYTHONPATH=src python -m aiq_kb.kb_cppn settle research/cppn_continual_20261101/seed_kb.json LAB_DIR/cppn_continual_db.jsonl
+
+No model is called. Assets are the Picbreeder genomes from akarshkumar0101/fer and dense networks trained in
+chengyingw/cppn-fer-experiments. These are toy results on one image per task and do not generalize beyond these networks.
